\section{Conclusion}
In this study, we have demonstrated the feasibility of using deep learning techniques to predict the likelihood of a patient developing COVID-19 based on their CT scan images. Our proposed model achieved an accuracy of $98\%$ and an AUC of $0.97$, demonstrating its effectiveness in distinguishing between positive and negative cases. This approach has the potential to aid in early diagnosis and timely intervention, ultimately contributing to better patient outcomes and reducing the burden on healthcare systems.

